  'Addressable LED strips for lighting, signage and displays. The current is far higher than people expect, around 60 mA per pixel at full white, and the far end of a long strip browns out and shifts colour before the supply gives up. It also flags the 3.3 V data problem, which is why these strips work intermittently with an ESP32.': 'Addressable LED strips for lighting, signage and displays. The current is far higher than people expect, around 60 mA per pixel at full white, and the far end of a long strip browns out and shifts colour before the supply gives up. It also flags the 3.3 V data problem, which is why these strips work intermittently with an ESP32.',
