  'Ampacity here is rule-of-thumb guidance, roughly 7.5 A/mm² for a single chassis run in free air and 3.5 A/mm² bundled. Real installations are governed by wiring regulations that account for insulation rating, grouping and ambient temperature. Use this to choose a starting point, not to certify an installation.': 'Ampacity here is rule-of-thumb guidance, roughly 7.5 A/mm² for a single chassis run in free air and 3.5 A/mm² bundled. Real installations are governed by wiring regulations that account for insulation rating, grouping and ambient temperature. Use this to choose a starting point, not to certify an installation.',
