  'Average current is the time-weighted mean over one cycle, `Iavg = (Ion·ton + Isleep·tsleep) / (ton + tsleep)`. Runtime is then the usable capacity divided by that. Nothing else matters: the peak current only affects whether the supply can deliver it, not how long the pack lasts.': 'Average current is the time-weighted mean over one cycle, `Iavg = (Ion·ton + Isleep·tsleep) / (ton + tsleep)`. Runtime is then the usable capacity divided by that. Nothing else matters: the peak current only affects whether the supply can deliver it, not how long the pack lasts.',
