  'Hang RL on it and the lower leg becomes `R2||RL`, giving `Vout = Vin·(R2||RL)/(R1 + R2||RL)`. Equivalently the source divides against its own impedance: `Vout·RL/(RL + Zout)`. The error is therefore `-Zout/(Zout + RL)`, which is -50% at RL = Zout, -9.1% at 10x and -1% at 100x.': 'Hang RL on it and the lower leg becomes `R2||RL`, giving `Vout = Vin·(R2||RL)/(R1 + R2||RL)`. Equivalently the source divides against its own impedance: `Vout·RL/(RL + Zout)`. The error is therefore `-Zout/(Zout + RL)`, which is -50% at RL = Zout, -9.1% at 10x and -1% at 100x.',
