  'Heat flow is the electrical analogy: power is current, temperature rise is voltage, thermal resistance in K/W is resistance. The three legs sit in series, so `Tj = Ta + P·(Rjc + Rcs + Rsa)`. Rjc comes from the package, Rcs from the mounting interface, Rsa from the heatsink and the air moving over it.': 'Heat flow is the electrical analogy: power is current, temperature rise is voltage, thermal resistance in K/W is resistance. The three legs sit in series, so `Tj = Ta + P·(Rjc + Rcs + Rsa)`. Rjc comes from the package, Rcs from the mounting interface, Rsa from the heatsink and the air moving over it.',
