  'Looking back into the output with the supply shorted, each pair is in parallel: `Rth = R1||R2 + R3||R4`. That is what a load sees, so a real load pulls the output down by `Rl/(Rth+Rl)`. Neither tap is at ground, so a single-ended ADC pin cannot read Vout directly, it needs a differential amplifier.': 'Looking back into the output with the supply shorted, each pair is in parallel: `Rth = R1||R2 + R3||R4`. That is what a load sees, so a real load pulls the output down by `Rl/(Rth+Rl)`. Neither tap is at ground, so a single-ended ADC pin cannot read Vout directly, it needs a differential amplifier.',
