  'Losses split three ways. Conduction is `Pcond = D·Id²·RDS(on)`. Crossover is `Psw = 0.5·VDS·Id·(tr + tf)·fsw`, taking each edge as a current rise at full voltage followed by a voltage fall at full current, which is the conservative clamped inductive case. Gate charge costs `Pgate = Qg·VGS·fsw`, dissipated in the gate resistor and the driving pin rather than in the FET. Only the first two heat the die, so `Tj = Ta + (Pcond + Psw)·Rth(j-a)`.': 'Losses split three ways. Conduction is `Pcond = D·Id²·RDS(on)`. Crossover is `Psw = 0.5·VDS·Id·(tr + tf)·fsw`, taking each edge as a current rise at full voltage followed by a voltage fall at full current, which is the conservative clamped inductive case. Gate charge costs `Pgate = Qg·VGS·fsw`, dissipated in the gate resistor and the driving pin rather than in the FET. Only the first two heat the die, so `Tj = Ta + (Pcond + Psw)·Rth(j-a)`.',
