  'Off-grid sensor nodes, weather stations and remote monitors. The failure mode it prevents is the system that breaks even on paper: it works all summer, then a cloudy week drains the battery and it never recovers, because the panel has no surplus to refill with.': 'Off-grid sensor nodes, weather stations and remote monitors. The failure mode it prevents is the system that breaks even on paper: it works all summer, then a cloudy week drains the battery and it never recovers, because the panel has no surplus to refill with.',
  'On the ESP32 the LEDC timer divides an 80 MHz clock into 2^bits steps per period, so frequency and duty resolution trade directly against each other. Push the frequency up and the resolution collapses. The scope shows the pin waveform and its average.': 'On the ESP32 the LEDC timer divides an 80 MHz clock into 2^bits steps per period, so frequency and duty resolution trade directly against each other. Push the frequency up and the resolution collapses. The scope shows the pin waveform and its average.',
  'On time': 'On time',
  'Once the valley current would go negative the diode has already turned off and the converter is in discontinuous conduction. The duty then follows from `Iout = Vin²·D²/(2·L·fsw·(Vout - Vin))`, i.e. `D = sqrt(2·L·fsw·Iout·(Vout - Vin))/Vin`. The boundary sits at `Iout = Vin·D(1-D)/(2·fsw·L)`.': 'Once the valley current would go negative the diode has already turned off and the converter is in discontinuous conduction. The duty then follows from `Iout = Vin²·D²/(2·L·fsw·(Vout - Vin))`, i.e. `D = sqrt(2·L·fsw·Iout·(Vout - Vin))/Vin`. The boundary sits at `Iout = Vin·D(1-D)/(2·fsw·L)`.',
  "One loop, so Kirchhoff gives `Vs = Vf + I·R` and the resistor follows from Ohm's law: `R = (Vs - Vf) / If`. The LED is modelled as a fixed forward drop, the standard piecewise-linear diode approximation. Above the knee its I-V curve is steep enough that Vf barely moves, so the resistor, not the diode, sets the current.": "One loop, so Kirchhoff gives `Vs = Vf + I·R` and the resistor follows from Ohm's law: `R = (Vs - Vf) / If`. The LED is modelled as a fixed forward drop, the standard piecewise-linear diode approximation. Above the knee its I-V curve is steep enough that Vf barely moves, so the resistor, not the diode, sets the current.",
  'One of the resistors is over its {rating} rating. Raise both values or move to a bigger package: the model is still linear, the part is not.': 'One of the resistors is over its {rating} rating. Raise both values or move to a bigger package: the model is still linear, the part is not.',
  'One PWM period is shorter than a scope sample at this time base, so the Vpwm trace is omitted rather than drawn aliased. Vout is a closed-form solution, so it stays exact.': 'One PWM period is shorter than a scope sample at this time base, so the Vpwm trace is omitted rather than drawn aliased. Vout is a closed-form solution, so it stays exact.',
  "One wiring note: the signal pin is happy at 3.3 V because servos read it as logic, but the motor itself wants 5 V or more and draws amps when stalled. Never power a servo from the ESP32 board's regulator, and keep the grounds common.": "One wiring note: the signal pin is happy at 3.3 V because servos read it as logic, but the motor itself wants 5 V or more and draws amps when stalled. Never power a servo from the ESP32 board's regulator, and keep the grounds common.",
  'Only {contactCurrent} flows through the contact. Dry switching below about 100 µA lets oxide build up on the contact faces, which eventually stops the switch working at all. Lower R if the switch is a mechanical one.': 'Only {contactCurrent} flows through the contact. Dry switching below about 100 µA lets oxide build up on the contact faces, which eventually stops the switch working at all. Lower R if the switch is a mechanical one.',
  'Only {headroom} across the resistor. Normal part to part Vf spread of {spread} then moves the current by {current}, so the resistor is barely in control. Raise the rail or use a constant current driver.': 'Only {headroom} across the resistor. Normal part to part Vf spread of {spread} then moves the current by {current}, so the resistor is barely in control. Raise the rail or use a constant current driver.',
  'Only {margin} K of margin. Tj max is an absolute maximum, not an operating point: leave {MARGIN_TARGET_K} K or more for part spread, a hot enclosure and a blocked airflow path.': 'Only {margin} K of margin. Tj max is an absolute maximum, not an operating point: leave {MARGIN_TARGET_K} K or more for part spread, a hot enclosure and a blocked airflow path.',
  'Only {marginDb} dB of margin. Free space loss is the best case: rain, foliage, a wall, a hand near the antenna or simple multipath fading each eat several dB. Aim for at least {MARGIN_MIN_DB} dB before calling a link dependable.': 'Only {marginDb} dB of margin. Free space loss is the best case: rain, foliage, a wall, a hand near the antenna or simple multipath fading each eat several dB. Aim for at least {MARGIN_MIN_DB} dB before calling a link dependable.',
  "Only {rangeUsed}% of the ADC range is in use, so most of the converter's resolution is wasted. Raise the gain until full-scale current lands near the top of the range.": "Only {rangeUsed}% of the ADC range is in use, so most of the converter's resolution is wasted. Raise the gain until full-scale current lands near the top of the range.",
  'Only {vgsMargin} of gate drive over the threshold. The FET turns on weakly and slowly, so edges degrade and the shifter becomes unreliable at temperature extremes where Vth shifts. Below about 1.8 V on the low side, use a dedicated shifter IC instead.': 'Only {vgsMargin} of gate drive over the threshold. The FET turns on weakly and slowly, so edges degrade and the shifter becomes unreliable at temperature extremes where Vth shifts. Below about 1.8 V on the low side, use a dedicated shifter IC instead.',
  'op-amp': 'op-amp',
  'Open drain means a device can only pull the line down. Releasing it leaves the bus capacitance to be charged through the pull-up, so the rising edge is an RC curve while the falling edge is nearly instant. Everything about pull-up sizing follows from that asymmetry.': 'Open drain means a device can only pull the line down. Releasing it leaves the bus capacitance to be charged through the pull-up, so the rising edge is an RC curve while the falling edge is nearly instant. Everything about pull-up sizing follows from that asymmetry.',
