  'Parallel branch network': 'Parallel branch network',
  "Parallel branches share a node voltage, so the current splits by conductance, not by resistance. The bar shows each branch's share of the total.": "Parallel branches share a node voltage, so the current splits by conductance, not by resistance. The bar shows each branch's share of the total.",
  'Parallel branches share one node pair, so they all see the same voltage. Conductance adds: `G = 1/R`, `Req = 1 / sum(G)`. Req is always smaller than the smallest branch, i.e. adding a path can only make the load heavier.': 'Parallel branches share one node pair, so they all see the same voltage. Conductance adds: `G = 1/R`, `Req = 1 / sum(G)`. Req is always smaller than the smallest branch, i.e. adding a path can only make the load heavier.',
  'Parallel capacitors add plate area, so `C = C1 + C2 + ...`. In series every capacitor carries the same charge and the voltages add, so `1/C = 1/C1 + 1/C2 + ...` and the total is smaller than the smallest member.': 'Parallel capacitors add plate area, so `C = C1 + C2 + ...`. In series every capacitor carries the same charge and the voltages add, so `1/C = 1/C1 + 1/C2 + ...` and the total is smaller than the smallest member.',
  'Parallel here is driven Thevenin style, i.e. the source feeds R in series into the L-C node. That is the same circuit as a current step `Vin/R` into R || L || C, so the parallel Q applies. Its output decays to zero because the inductor is a short at DC.': 'Parallel here is driven Thevenin style, i.e. the source feeds R in series into the L-C node. That is the same circuit as a current step `Vin/R` into R || L || C, so the parallel Q applies. Its output decays to zero because the inductor is a short at DC.',
