  'Peak inverse voltage is what actually kills diodes. A bridge diode blocks one `Vpeak`. A half wave or centre tapped diode has the negative peak on its anode while the cap holds its cathode at `Vdc`, so it blocks `Vpeak + Vdc`, i.e. about `2·Vpeak`. A 12 V secondary is already 34 V of PIV.': 'Peak inverse voltage is what actually kills diodes. A bridge diode blocks one `Vpeak`. A half wave or centre tapped diode has the negative peak on its anode while the cap holds its cathode at `Vdc`, so it blocks `Vpeak + Vdc`, i.e. about `2·Vpeak`. A 12 V secondary is already 34 V of PIV.',
