  'R sets how fast the stored energy leaks away. Series: `Q = (1/R)·sqrt(L/C)` and `alpha = R / (2L)`. Parallel: `Q = R·sqrt(C/L)` and `alpha = 1 / (2·R·C)`. The two are reciprocal about the characteristic impedance `Z0 = sqrt(L/C)`, so series wants R small for a high Q and parallel wants R large.': 'R sets how fast the stored energy leaks away. Series: `Q = (1/R)·sqrt(L/C)` and `alpha = R / (2L)`. Parallel: `Q = R·sqrt(C/L)` and `alpha = 1 / (2·R·C)`. The two are reciprocal about the characteristic impedance `Z0 = sqrt(L/C)`, so series wants R small for a high Q and parallel wants R large.',
