  'RDS(on) is not a constant. Deep in triode the channel is `rds = 1 / (k·Vov)`, so a datasheet quote pins down k: `k = 1 / (RDS(on)spec · (VGSspec - Vth))`, and at any other gate voltage `RDS(on) = RDS(on)spec · (VGSspec - Vth) / (VGS - Vth)`. That is why a part advertised at 22 mΩ is nearer 51 mΩ on 3.3 V, and why a part quoted at 10 V is simply off.': 'RDS(on) is not a constant. Deep in triode the channel is `rds = 1 / (k·Vov)`, so a datasheet quote pins down k: `k = 1 / (RDS(on)spec · (VGSspec - Vth))`, and at any other gate voltage `RDS(on) = RDS(on)spec · (VGSspec - Vth) / (VGS - Vth)`. That is why a part advertised at 22 mΩ is nearer 51 mΩ on 3.3 V, and why a part quoted at 10 V is simply off.',
  'RDS(on) quoted': 'RDS(on) quoted',
  'Reactance': 'Reactance',
  'Reactance is frequency dependent: `XL = 2·pi·f·L` rises with frequency and `XC = 1/(2·pi·f·C)` falls. Written as complex impedances they are `+jXL` and `-jXC`, so they subtract rather than add, and at one particular frequency they cancel entirely.': 'Reactance is frequency dependent: `XL = 2·pi·f·L` rises with frequency and `XC = 1/(2·pi·f·C)` falls. Written as complex impedances they are `+jXL` and `-jXC`, so they subtract rather than add, and at one particular frequency they cancel entirely.',
