  'SMD codes work the same way. Three digits is two figures plus an exponent, so 472 is 47 × 10², i.e. 4.7 kΩ. Four digits is three figures plus an exponent, so 4701 is 470 × 10¹, also 4.7 kΩ. Note the last digit is never a zero of the value itself, which catches people out constantly.': 'SMD codes work the same way. Three digits is two figures plus an exponent, so 472 is 47 × 10², i.e. 4.7 kΩ. Four digits is three figures plus an exponent, so 4701 is 470 × 10¹, also 4.7 kΩ. Note the last digit is never a zero of the value itself, which catches people out constantly.',
