  'Steady-state inductor current in a step-up converter. The horizontal axis is time, a few switching periods wide. Sky is the inductor, green is what the switch pulls to ground, amber is what the diode hands to the output cap: the gap between those two is why the input current runs higher than the output current.': 'Steady-state inductor current in a step-up converter. The horizontal axis is time, a few switching periods wide. Sky is the inductor, green is what the switch pulls to ground, amber is what the diode hands to the output cap: the gap between those two is why the input current runs higher than the output current.',
