  'Stepping a higher rail down efficiently: 12 V to 5 V, 5 V to 3.3 V, battery to logic. This is how nearly every ESP32 board makes its 3.3 V rail from USB. The inductor ripple and CCM/DCM boundary decide whether the converter is quiet and well behaved or noisy and load dependent.': 'Stepping a higher rail down efficiently: 12 V to 5 V, 5 V to 3.3 V, battery to logic. This is how nearly every ESP32 board makes its 3.3 V rail from USB. The inductor ripple and CCM/DCM boundary decide whether the converter is quiet and well behaved or noisy and load dependent.',
